Z||000000||Stoic||01-26-2001||09:54 PM||||I'm considering buying an '85 GT, 6cyl./4 spd<BR>I havent seen it yet, but the guy claims that the only thing wrong with it is the transmission.  If the car is worth buying, I was hoping to put in a 5spd. I know it will bolt on, but can I just bolt it on and go, or are there certain details I'm not aware of?  Obviously aside from the centre console piece.  <BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mi Junk||01-27-2001||10:33 AM||||You have to change the shifter and the cables. I think the hydru. are the same.<BR>If you don't pick it up let me know. I'm still looking for a project car. Thinking maybe a SPYDER.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Stoic||01-27-2001||01:31 PM||||That helps, thanks.  If you have any idea on cost to have one put in at a shop that'd be helpful too.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||6
Z||000003||JimIndyRCR||01-27-2001||01:35 PM||||I just did this very swap last summer. <BR>You will have to change the shifter & cables. Make sure you get the rubber grommets (that insulate the cables through the 'firewall') with the cables (they are different with the 5 spd cables). After trying many combinations for the hydraulics I eventually went with the original 4 spd master & original 4spd slave cylinder (clutch action is perfect!!) -you will have to punch out the studs on the original 4spd slave because the 5 spd comes with studs on the tranny. Everything else is a simple bolt together. The backup light switch is on the shifter with the 4 speed and the trans with the 5 spd...............so I ran 2 wires from the back up switch at the trans and spliced them into the wires that went to the 4 spd switch and voila - backup lights too. It's the most beneficial swap I've ever done-changed the way the car drives completely-in a good way!!<BR>any more questions feel free to contact me directly,<BR>Jim||||reg||1
